1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,253
A developer changes one line,

2
00:00:02,253 --> 00:00:03,583
on a Friday afternoon.

3
00:00:03,583 --> 00:00:05,033
Nothing looks different.

4
00:00:05,033 --> 00:00:05,940
Do you ship it?

5
00:00:06,490 --> 00:00:09,729
A team that does not test finds out from its customers.

6
00:00:09,729 --> 00:00:12,262
A team that tests finds out in two minutes,

7
00:00:12,262 --> 00:00:13,381
before anyone else.

8
00:00:13,931 --> 00:00:15,999
But not every test is the same.

9
00:00:15,999 --> 00:00:17,601
Some take a millisecond.

10
00:00:17,601 --> 00:00:20,136
Some open a browser and take a minute.

11
00:00:20,136 --> 00:00:22,805
Some only ask one question: is it alive?

12
00:00:23,355 --> 00:00:25,633
Today you learn the six kinds of test,

13
00:00:25,633 --> 00:00:26,892
what each one is for,

14
00:00:26,892 --> 00:00:28,031
and when to run it.

15
00:00:28,031 --> 00:00:30,609
Then you sort a real set of tests yourself.

16
00:00:32,159 --> 00:00:33,588
Here is what to expect.

17
00:00:34,138 --> 00:00:35,632
One: the test pyramid.

18
00:00:35,632 --> 00:00:39,910
A picture of how many tests of each kind a healthy project has,

19
00:00:39,910 --> 00:00:40,453
and why.

20
00:00:41,003 --> 00:00:42,935
Two: the six kinds of test.

21
00:00:42,935 --> 00:00:43,293
Unit,

22
00:00:43,293 --> 00:00:44,152
integration,

23
00:00:44,152 --> 00:00:44,438
API,

24
00:00:44,438 --> 00:00:45,226
end to end,

25
00:00:45,226 --> 00:00:45,655
smoke,

26
00:00:45,655 --> 00:00:46,729
and regression.

27
00:00:46,729 --> 00:00:48,232
What each one checks,

28
00:00:48,232 --> 00:00:49,878
and what it cannot see.

29
00:00:50,428 --> 00:00:52,348
Three: when to run which test.

30
00:00:52,348 --> 00:00:53,372
On every commit,

31
00:00:53,372 --> 00:00:54,780
on every pull request,

32
00:00:54,780 --> 00:00:56,124
before every release,

33
00:00:56,124 --> 00:00:57,404
and after every bug.

34
00:00:57,954 --> 00:00:59,124
Four: a live demo,

35
00:00:59,124 --> 00:01:00,034
with pie test,

36
00:01:00,034 --> 00:01:01,334
on a real mini shop.

37
00:01:01,334 --> 00:01:02,569
You run every kind,

38
00:01:02,569 --> 00:01:06,274
and watch the difference in speed and in what they touch.

39
00:01:06,824 --> 00:01:12,178
Then your turn: a lab with six checks. This is lesson one of the software testing domain.

40
00:01:14,228 --> 00:01:18,793
The test pyramid. One picture, and it explains a whole testing strategy.

41
00:01:19,343 --> 00:01:20,990
At the bottom: unit tests.

42
00:01:20,990 --> 00:01:23,142
They test one small piece of code,

43
00:01:23,142 --> 00:01:23,522
alone.

44
00:01:23,522 --> 00:01:24,409
They are fast,

45
00:01:24,409 --> 00:01:25,802
a millisecond or less,

46
00:01:25,802 --> 00:01:27,005
and cheap to write.

47
00:01:27,005 --> 00:01:29,221
A healthy project has many of them.

48
00:01:29,771 --> 00:01:32,499
In the middle: integration and API tests.

49
00:01:32,499 --> 00:01:36,226
They test pieces working together: code with a database,

50
00:01:36,226 --> 00:01:38,090
or a request to an endpoint.

51
00:01:38,090 --> 00:01:38,556
Slower,

52
00:01:38,556 --> 00:01:39,221
and fewer.

53
00:01:39,771 --> 00:01:41,560
At the top: end to end tests.

54
00:01:41,560 --> 00:01:44,459
They walk through the whole system like a user.

55
00:01:44,459 --> 00:01:45,754
They are the slowest,

56
00:01:45,754 --> 00:01:47,049
and the most fragile,

57
00:01:47,049 --> 00:01:48,838
so a healthy project has few.

58
00:01:49,388 --> 00:01:50,727
Going up the pyramid,

59
00:01:50,727 --> 00:01:53,149
a test covers more of the real system,

60
00:01:53,149 --> 00:01:54,935
so it gives more confidence.

61
00:01:54,935 --> 00:01:56,018
But it is slower,

62
00:01:56,018 --> 00:01:57,421
it breaks more easily,

63
00:01:57,421 --> 00:01:58,568
and when it fails,

64
00:01:58,568 --> 00:02:00,417
it is harder to find out why.

65
00:02:00,967 --> 00:02:01,605
Going down,

66
00:02:01,605 --> 00:02:04,504
a test is fast and points straight at the problem,

67
00:02:04,504 --> 00:02:06,301
but it sees only a small piece.

68
00:02:06,851 --> 00:02:12,184
So you want both: many small fast tests for speed, and a few big tests for confidence.

69
00:02:13,734 --> 00:02:16,209
The six kinds of test. One at a time.

70
00:02:16,759 --> 00:02:17,416
Unit test.

71
00:02:17,416 --> 00:02:19,716
It tests one function or one class,

72
00:02:19,716 --> 00:02:20,110
alone,

73
00:02:20,110 --> 00:02:21,227
with no database,

74
00:02:21,227 --> 00:02:21,950
no network,

75
00:02:21,950 --> 00:02:22,805
and no files.

76
00:02:22,805 --> 00:02:27,865
In our shop: does line total give two thousand nine hundred and ninety-seven,

77
00:02:27,865 --> 00:02:28,850
for three mugs?

78
00:02:28,850 --> 00:02:30,493
It runs in a millisecond.

79
00:02:30,493 --> 00:02:31,413
When it fails,

80
00:02:31,413 --> 00:02:33,911
you know exactly which function broke.

81
00:02:34,461 --> 00:02:35,537
Integration test.

82
00:02:35,537 --> 00:02:39,272
It tests your code together with a real part it depends on,

83
00:02:39,272 --> 00:02:40,664
most often a database.

84
00:02:40,664 --> 00:02:42,880
Does the cart total come out right,

85
00:02:42,880 --> 00:02:46,045
when the items are really stored and loaded again?

86
00:02:46,045 --> 00:02:46,868
It is slower,

87
00:02:46,868 --> 00:02:50,223
but it catches what unit tests cannot: wrong queries,

88
00:02:50,223 --> 00:02:51,109
wrong columns,

89
00:02:51,109 --> 00:02:51,869
wrong types.

90
00:02:52,419 --> 00:02:53,019
API test.

91
00:02:53,019 --> 00:02:56,022
It sends a real request to a running service,

92
00:02:56,022 --> 00:02:58,624
and checks the answer: the status code,

93
00:02:58,624 --> 00:02:59,492
and the body.

94
00:02:59,492 --> 00:03:02,761
Does slash API slash products return two hundred,

95
00:03:02,761 --> 00:03:04,096
with three products?

96
00:03:04,096 --> 00:03:06,698
Does a bad product return four hundred?

97
00:03:06,698 --> 00:03:10,168
It tests the contract that other programs depend on.

98
00:03:10,718 --> 00:03:11,777
End to end test.

99
00:03:11,777 --> 00:03:13,167
A whole user journey,

100
00:03:13,167 --> 00:03:14,822
through the whole system.

101
00:03:14,822 --> 00:03:16,213
Look at the products,

102
00:03:16,213 --> 00:03:16,875
add a mug,

103
00:03:16,875 --> 00:03:17,603
add a lamp,

104
00:03:17,603 --> 00:03:18,265
check out,

105
00:03:18,265 --> 00:03:20,251
and confirm the cart is empty.

106
00:03:20,251 --> 00:03:21,509
The most realistic,

107
00:03:21,509 --> 00:03:22,568
and the slowest.

108
00:03:22,568 --> 00:03:25,613
Real projects often drive a real browser here.

109
00:03:25,613 --> 00:03:26,209
You will,

110
00:03:26,209 --> 00:03:27,401
in a later lesson.

111
00:03:27,951 --> 00:03:28,703
Smoke test.

112
00:03:28,703 --> 00:03:29,181
A tiny,

113
00:03:29,181 --> 00:03:31,643
fast check that the system is alive,

114
00:03:31,643 --> 00:03:33,968
and its most important parts work.

115
00:03:33,968 --> 00:03:35,609
Is the health page okay?

116
00:03:35,609 --> 00:03:37,318
Is the catalog not empty?

117
00:03:37,318 --> 00:03:41,489
Named after switching on new electronics: if smoke comes out,

118
00:03:41,489 --> 00:03:41,831
stop.

119
00:03:41,831 --> 00:03:44,292
You run it right after every deploy.

120
00:03:44,842 --> 00:03:45,861
Regression test.

121
00:03:45,861 --> 00:03:47,580
Not a level of the pyramid,

122
00:03:47,580 --> 00:03:48,472
but a purpose.

123
00:03:48,472 --> 00:03:50,382
When a bug is found and fixed,

124
00:03:50,382 --> 00:03:52,993
you write a test that fails with the bug,

125
00:03:52,993 --> 00:03:54,521
and passes with the fix.

126
00:03:54,521 --> 00:03:55,604
It stays forever,

127
00:03:55,604 --> 00:03:58,278
so that bug can never come back unnoticed.

128
00:03:58,278 --> 00:04:00,634
A regression test can be a unit test,

129
00:04:00,634 --> 00:04:01,781
or any other kind.

130
00:04:02,331 --> 00:04:03,227
Notice: unit,

131
00:04:03,227 --> 00:04:04,054
integration,

132
00:04:04,054 --> 00:04:08,743
API and end to end tell you how much of the system the test touches.

133
00:04:08,743 --> 00:04:11,845
Smoke and regression tell you why you run it.

134
00:04:13,395 --> 00:04:17,512
When do you run which test? Fast tests often. Slow tests wisely.

135
00:04:18,062 --> 00:04:19,894
On every commit: unit tests,

136
00:04:19,894 --> 00:04:21,399
and a quick smoke test.

137
00:04:21,399 --> 00:04:22,316
A few seconds.

138
00:04:22,316 --> 00:04:24,737
A developer runs them before pushing,

139
00:04:24,737 --> 00:04:25,849
many times a day.

140
00:04:26,399 --> 00:04:31,055
On every pull request: add the integration tests and the API tests.

141
00:04:31,055 --> 00:04:32,029
A few minutes,

142
00:04:32,029 --> 00:04:33,488
run by the CI server,

143
00:04:33,488 --> 00:04:35,295
so nobody has to remember.

144
00:04:35,845 --> 00:04:38,673
Before a release: add the end to end tests,

145
00:04:38,673 --> 00:04:39,594
the slow ones.

146
00:04:39,594 --> 00:04:42,620
And right after every deploy: the smoke tests,

147
00:04:42,620 --> 00:04:44,528
against the real environment.

148
00:04:45,078 --> 00:04:47,611
After every bug: a new regression test,

149
00:04:47,611 --> 00:04:48,521
written first.

150
00:04:48,521 --> 00:04:49,496
The test fails,

151
00:04:49,496 --> 00:04:50,600
you fix the code,

152
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:51,640
the test passes,

153
00:04:51,640 --> 00:04:53,654
and it joins the suite forever.

154
00:04:54,204 --> 00:04:57,216
This is how a pipeline gets both speed and safety.

155
00:04:57,216 --> 00:04:59,686
We build that pipeline in a later lesson.

156
00:05:01,236 --> 00:05:06,420
Go to the lab folder.

157
00:05:07,970 --> 00:05:09,869
Look around.

158
00:05:10,419 --> 00:05:15,965
A small shop module, a shared setup file, and a folder of tests. Let us look at the tests.

159
00:05:16,515 --> 00:05:17,945
The tests folder.

160
00:05:18,795 --> 00:05:19,585
Five files.

161
00:05:19,585 --> 00:05:20,087
Prices,

162
00:05:20,087 --> 00:05:21,093
cart database,

163
00:05:21,093 --> 00:05:21,380
API,

164
00:05:21,380 --> 00:05:21,955
journey,

165
00:05:21,955 --> 00:05:22,745
and health.

166
00:05:22,745 --> 00:05:25,474
Every one is a different kind of test.

167
00:05:25,474 --> 00:05:27,413
Your task is to tell which.

168
00:05:27,963 --> 00:05:34,982
A unit test file.

169
00:05:35,532 --> 00:05:36,588
Plain functions.

170
00:05:36,588 --> 00:05:38,965
Each calls one function of the shop,

171
00:05:38,965 --> 00:05:40,285
with simple numbers,

172
00:05:40,285 --> 00:05:41,803
and asserts the answer.

173
00:05:41,803 --> 00:05:42,595
No database,

174
00:05:42,595 --> 00:05:43,321
no network.

175
00:05:43,321 --> 00:05:44,641
That is a unit test.

176
00:05:45,191 --> 00:05:47,943
Run it.

177
00:05:48,993 --> 00:05:49,767
Five passed,

178
00:05:49,767 --> 00:05:51,829
in a few hundredths of a second.

179
00:05:51,829 --> 00:05:53,182
Each dot is one test.

180
00:05:53,182 --> 00:05:55,244
That is the speed of unit tests.

181
00:05:55,794 --> 00:06:01,767
An integration test.

182
00:06:02,317 --> 00:06:03,235
Three passed.

183
00:06:03,235 --> 00:06:05,774
Each test gets a real database file,

184
00:06:05,774 --> 00:06:07,327
in a temporary folder,

185
00:06:07,327 --> 00:06:09,302
created for it by a fixture.

186
00:06:09,302 --> 00:06:10,219
Real queries,

187
00:06:10,219 --> 00:06:11,137
real storage.

188
00:06:11,137 --> 00:06:13,112
That is an integration test.

189
00:06:13,662 --> 00:06:17,587
An API test.

190
00:06:18,437 --> 00:06:19,325
Three passed.

191
00:06:19,325 --> 00:06:22,398
Each one starts a real server on a free port,

192
00:06:22,398 --> 00:06:23,969
sends H T T P requests,

193
00:06:23,969 --> 00:06:25,813
and checks the status code.

194
00:06:25,813 --> 00:06:26,633
Two hundred,

195
00:06:26,633 --> 00:06:27,520
four hundred,

196
00:06:27,520 --> 00:06:29,296
and four hundred and nine.

197
00:06:29,846 --> 00:06:35,457
End to end.

198
00:06:36,007 --> 00:06:36,613
One test,

199
00:06:36,613 --> 00:06:37,892
many steps: browse,

200
00:06:37,892 --> 00:06:38,835
add two items,

201
00:06:38,835 --> 00:06:39,912
check the total,

202
00:06:39,912 --> 00:06:40,181
pay,

203
00:06:40,181 --> 00:06:42,403
and check that the cart is empty.

204
00:06:42,403 --> 00:06:43,480
One failed step,

205
00:06:43,480 --> 00:06:45,163
and the whole test fails.

206
00:06:45,163 --> 00:06:47,655
That is why end to end tests are few.

207
00:06:48,205 --> 00:06:53,559
Smoke.

208
00:06:54,109 --> 00:06:56,120
Two quick checks: the health page,

209
00:06:56,120 --> 00:06:58,013
and a catalog that is not empty.

210
00:06:58,013 --> 00:06:58,841
If these fail,

211
00:06:58,841 --> 00:07:00,083
nothing else matters.

212
00:07:00,633 --> 00:07:10,403
A bug report.

213
00:07:10,953 --> 00:07:12,016
Eight ninety-nine.

214
00:07:12,016 --> 00:07:13,551
The fixed code is correct.

215
00:07:13,551 --> 00:07:15,558
Now bring the bug back on purpose,

216
00:07:15,558 --> 00:07:17,033
with the shop bug switch.

217
00:07:17,583 --> 00:07:21,765
With the bug.

218
00:07:25,315 --> 00:07:26,132
Nine hundred,

219
00:07:26,132 --> 00:07:27,578
in cents: nine dollars.

220
00:07:27,578 --> 00:07:28,772
That is bug twelve.

221
00:07:28,772 --> 00:07:31,224
The discount was rounded the wrong way.

222
00:07:31,774 --> 00:07:37,833
Register markers.

223
00:07:44,583 --> 00:07:45,382
Six markers,

224
00:07:45,382 --> 00:07:46,581
one for each kind,

225
00:07:46,581 --> 00:07:47,846
and strict markers.

226
00:07:47,846 --> 00:07:50,843
Strict means a misspelled marker is an error,

227
00:07:50,843 --> 00:07:52,241
not a silent mistake.

228
00:07:52,791 --> 00:07:58,338
Write the test.

229
00:08:06,688 --> 00:08:09,150
The marker says what kind of test this is.

230
00:08:09,150 --> 00:08:14,368
The assert says what must be true: ten percent off nine ninety-nine is eight ninety-nine.

231
00:08:14,918 --> 00:08:18,651
Fails with the bug.

232
00:08:21,001 --> 00:08:26,228
Red. One failed: nine hundred is not eight ninety-nine. The test catches the bug.

233
00:08:26,778 --> 00:08:30,362
Passes without.

234
00:08:30,912 --> 00:08:34,539
Green. One passed. This test now guards that bug forever.

235
00:08:35,089 --> 00:08:38,737
Everything.

236
00:08:39,287 --> 00:08:40,167
Fifteen passed.

237
00:08:40,167 --> 00:08:42,337
But all the kinds are mixed together.

238
00:08:42,337 --> 00:08:44,508
How would you run only the fast ones?

239
00:08:44,508 --> 00:08:45,857
You need to label them.

240
00:08:46,407 --> 00:08:51,698
Label the unit tests.

241
00:08:53,348 --> 00:08:57,167
Run only unit tests.

242
00:08:57,717 --> 00:08:58,542
Five passed,

243
00:08:58,542 --> 00:08:59,573
ten deselected.

244
00:08:59,573 --> 00:09:01,222
Only the unit tests ran.

245
00:09:01,222 --> 00:09:05,141
That is the power of a label: you choose which tests run.

246
00:09:05,691 --> 00:09:10,768
Everything else.

247
00:09:11,318 --> 00:09:14,091
Ten passed. Same suite, a different slice.

248
00:09:14,641 --> 00:09:17,009
Run the judge.

249
00:09:17,559 --> 00:09:19,435
Three checks pass: the markers,

250
00:09:19,435 --> 00:09:20,343
the unit tests,

251
00:09:20,343 --> 00:09:21,795
and the regression test.

252
00:09:21,795 --> 00:09:23,006
Three are still red,

253
00:09:23,006 --> 00:09:25,729
because the other files are not labelled yet.

254
00:09:25,729 --> 00:09:26,818
That is your task.

255
00:09:27,368 --> 00:09:29,331
Clean up.

256
00:09:29,881 --> 00:09:31,737
Removed. Nothing left behind.

257
00:09:33,287 --> 00:09:37,362
Your lab task: classify the tests of the mini shop. Six checks.

258
00:09:37,912 --> 00:09:42,861
One: register the six markers in pie test dot I N I, with strict markers.

259
00:09:43,411 --> 00:09:45,998
Two: label every test with its kind.

260
00:09:45,998 --> 00:09:46,717
Five unit,

261
00:09:46,717 --> 00:09:48,011
three integration,

262
00:09:48,011 --> 00:09:48,729
three API,

263
00:09:48,729 --> 00:09:49,807
one end to end,

264
00:09:49,807 --> 00:09:50,814
and two smoke.

265
00:09:51,364 --> 00:09:53,195
Three: bug twelve is in the lab.

266
00:09:53,195 --> 00:09:54,683
Write the regression test.

267
00:09:54,683 --> 00:09:56,171
It must fail with the bug,

268
00:09:56,171 --> 00:09:57,316
and pass without it.

269
00:09:57,866 --> 00:10:00,191
Then lab check, until six out of six.

270
00:10:02,241 --> 00:10:05,036
Where to find the lab. Pause here, and write it down.

271
00:10:05,586 --> 00:10:07,050
One: the repository,

272
00:10:07,050 --> 00:10:11,370
git hub dot com slash it dash waves slash dev ops dash A I,

273
00:10:11,370 --> 00:10:13,714
in the folder academy slash lab.

274
00:10:14,264 --> 00:10:20,386
Two: the files, lab one thirty-five dot S H, and shortcuts one thirty-five dot S H.

275
00:10:20,936 --> 00:10:26,398
Three: install it, with sudo install, into slash user slash local slash S bin.

276
00:10:26,948 --> 00:10:28,772
Four: load the short names,

277
00:10:28,772 --> 00:10:31,879
with source shortcuts one thirty-five dot S H.

278
00:10:31,879 --> 00:10:32,690
Then lab up,

279
00:10:32,690 --> 00:10:33,365
lab check,

280
00:10:33,365 --> 00:10:34,244
and lab down.

281
00:10:34,794 --> 00:10:37,797
Five: you need python three and pie test.

282
00:10:37,797 --> 00:10:38,529
On Ubuntu,

283
00:10:38,529 --> 00:10:39,774
sudo apt install,

284
00:10:39,774 --> 00:10:40,726
python three,

285
00:10:40,726 --> 00:10:41,386
pie test.

